IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc-core-persons`
IMPORT `uc4-part8-ch1-carers-hours`
IMPORT `uc4-part8-ch1-groups`

-- Part 8 of the Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/376), Chapter 1, regulations 93 to 98: the purposes of a work-focused
-- interview, when a claimant is treated as not having complied with a work search or work availability requirement, the limitations on
-- those requirements, and the effect of domestic violence.
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2013-376.txt, a plain-text rendering of the revised text (legislation.gov.uk, version 2026-07-16)
-- made by a converter script. It is not the official text. Every `-- src:N | ...` line copies line N of that file.
-- Target: the stable build 1.6.98. Seat: a person who claims or receives Universal Credit (see uc4-seat.l4).
--
-- WHO DECIDES. "The Secretary of State is satisfied", "agreed by the Secretary of State" and "the Secretary of State considers" are
-- stated BOOLEAN or NUMBER inputs worded as the text words them. Where a provision says the Secretary of State "must not impose" a
-- requirement, the rule says whether that is so on the facts given; nothing here imposes anything.

§ `The work-related requirements`

-- src:1449 | The work-related requirements

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulation 93 — Purposes of a work-focused interview`

-- The purposes of a work-focused interview are any or all of six. A purpose that is none of them is not a purpose of a work-focused interview.
-- src:1450 | 93 Purposes of a work-focused interview
-- src:1451 | The purposes of a work-focused interview are any or all of the following—
-- src:1452 | (a) assessing the claimant's prospects for remaining in or obtaining paid work;
-- src:1453 | (b) assisting or encouraging the claimant to remain in or obtain paid work;
-- src:1454 | (c) identifying activities that the claimant may undertake that will make remaining in or obtaining paid work more likely;
-- src:1455 | (d) identifying training, educational or rehabilitation opportunities for the claimant which may make it more likely that the claimant will remain in or obtain paid work or be able to do so;
-- src:1456 | (e) identifying current or future work opportunities for the claimant that are relevant to the claimant's needs and abilities;
-- src:1457 | (f) ascertaining whether a claimant is in gainful self-employment or meets the conditions in regulation 63 (start-up period).
@ref reg 93 (src:1450-1457)
DECLARE `Purpose of a work-focused interview` IS ONE OF
    `assessing the claimant's prospects for remaining in or obtaining paid work`
    `assisting or encouraging the claimant to remain in or obtain paid work`
    `identifying activities that the claimant may undertake that will make remaining in or obtaining paid work more likely`
    `identifying training, educational or rehabilitation opportunities for the claimant which may make it more likely that the claimant will remain in or obtain paid work or be able to do so`
    `identifying current or future work opportunities for the claimant that are relevant to the claimant's needs and abilities`
    `ascertaining whether a claimant is in gainful self-employment or meets the conditions in regulation 63 (start-up period)`

@ref reg 93 (src:1450-1457)
GIVEN purposes IS A LIST OF `Purpose of a work-focused interview`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 93 — the interview has a purpose of a work-focused interview` purposes MEANS
    NOT (null purposes)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulation 94 — Work search requirement - interviews`

-- A claimant is treated as not having complied with a work search requirement to apply for a particular vacancy for paid work where the
-- claimant fails to participate in an interview offered in connection with the vacancy.
-- src:1458 | 94 Work search requirement - interviews
-- src:1459 | A claimant is to be treated as not having complied with a work search requirement to apply for a particular vacancy for paid work where the claimant fails to participate in an interview offered to the claimant in connection with the vacancy.
@ref reg 94 (src:1458-1459)
GIVEN `an interview was offered to the claimant in connection with the vacancy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant fails to participate in the interview` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 94 — the claimant is treated as not having complied with a work search requirement to apply for a vacancy` `an interview was offered to the claimant in connection with the vacancy` `the claimant fails to participate in the interview` MEANS
    `an interview was offered to the claimant in connection with the vacancy`
    AND `the claimant fails to participate in the interview`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulation 95 — Work search requirement - all reasonable action`

-- Paragraph (4): "voluntary work preparation" is particular action taken by a claimant and agreed by the Secretary of State for the purpose of
-- making it more likely that the claimant will obtain paid work, but not specified by the Secretary of State as a work preparation
-- requirement under section 16 of the Act.
-- out of range: sections 15 to 18 and 23 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (not among the inputs): which requirement is in question, and its limits, are stated inputs
-- src:1470 | (4) “Voluntary work preparation” means particular action taken by a claimant and agreed by the Secretary of State for the purpose of making it more likely that the claimant will obtain paid work, but which is not specified by the Secretary of State as a work preparation requirement under section 16 of the Act.
@ref reg 95(4) (src:1470)
GIVEN `particular action taken by the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action is agreed by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action is for the purpose of making it more likely that the claimant will obtain paid work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action is specified by the Secretary of State as a work preparation requirement under section 16 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 95(4) — voluntary work preparation` `particular action taken by the claimant` `the action is agreed by the Secretary of State` `the action is for the purpose of making it more likely that the claimant will obtain paid work` `the action is specified by the Secretary of State as a work preparation requirement under section 16 of the Act` MEANS
    `particular action taken by the claimant`
    AND `the action is agreed by the Secretary of State`
    AND `the action is for the purpose of making it more likely that the claimant will obtain paid work`
    AND (NOT `the action is specified by the Secretary of State as a work preparation requirement under section 16 of the Act`)

-- Paragraphs (2) and (3): the relevant deductions are the total of the time agreed by the Secretary of State (a) for the claimant to carry out
-- paid work, voluntary work, a work preparation requirement, or voluntary work preparation in that week, or (b) to deal with temporary
-- childcare responsibilities, a domestic emergency, funeral arrangements or other temporary circumstances; the time agreed for voluntary
-- work must not exceed 50% of the expected number of hours per week, so any more is not counted. All times are hours in the week.
-- src:1466 | (2) In this regulation “relevant deductions” means the total of any time agreed by the Secretary of State—
-- src:1467 | (a) for the claimant to carry out paid work, voluntary work, a work preparation requirement, or voluntary work preparation in that week; or
-- src:1468 | (b) for the claimant to deal with temporary childcare responsibilities, a domestic emergency, funeral arrangements or other temporary circumstances.
-- src:1469 | (3) For the purpose of paragraph (2)(a) the time agreed by the Secretary of State for the claimant to carry out voluntary work must not exceed 50% of the claimant's expected number of hours per week.
@ref reg 95(2) and (3) (src:1466-1469)
GIVEN `hours agreed for the claimant to carry out paid work` IS A NUMBER
      `hours agreed for the claimant to carry out voluntary work` IS A NUMBER
      `hours agreed for the claimant to carry out a work preparation requirement` IS A NUMBER
      `hours agreed for the claimant to carry out voluntary work preparation` IS A NUMBER
      `hours agreed for the claimant to deal with temporary childcare responsibilities, a domestic emergency, funeral arrangements or other temporary circumstances` IS A NUMBER
      `the expected number of hours per week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 95(2) and (3) — the relevant deductions` `hours agreed for the claimant to carry out paid work` `hours agreed for the claimant to carry out voluntary work` `hours agreed for the claimant to carry out a work preparation requirement` `hours agreed for the claimant to carry out voluntary work preparation` `hours agreed for the claimant to deal with temporary childcare responsibilities, a domestic emergency, funeral arrangements or other temporary circumstances` `the expected number of hours per week` MEANS
    `hours agreed for the claimant to carry out paid work`
    PLUS (minimum (LIST `hours agreed for the claimant to carry out voluntary work`, (`the expected number of hours per week` TIMES 0.5)))
    PLUS `hours agreed for the claimant to carry out a work preparation requirement`
    PLUS `hours agreed for the claimant to carry out voluntary work preparation`
    PLUS `hours agreed for the claimant to deal with temporary childcare responsibilities, a domestic emergency, funeral arrangements or other temporary circumstances`

-- Paragraph (1): a claimant is treated as not having complied with a work search requirement to take all reasonable action for the purpose of
-- obtaining paid work in any week unless (a) either (i) the time spent taking action is at least the expected number of hours per week minus
-- any relevant deductions, or (ii) the Secretary of State is satisfied that the claimant has taken all reasonable action despite fewer hours;
-- and (b) that action gives the claimant the best prospects of obtaining work.
-- src:1460 | 95 Work search requirement - all reasonable action
-- src:1461 | (1) A claimant is to be treated as not having complied with a work search requirement to take all reasonable action for the purpose of obtaining paid work in any week unless—
-- src:1462 | (a) either—
-- src:1463 | (i) the time which the claimant spends taking action for the purpose of obtaining paid work is at least the claimant's expected number of hours per week minus any relevant deductions, or
-- src:1464 | (ii) the Secretary of State is satisfied that the claimant has taken all reasonable action for the purpose of obtaining paid work despite the number of hours that the claimant spends taking such action being lower than the expected number of hours per week; and
-- src:1465 | (b) that action gives the claimant the best prospects of obtaining work.
@ref reg 95(1) (src:1460-1465)
GIVEN `the time which the claimant spends taking action for the purpose of obtaining paid work` IS A NUMBER
      `the expected number of hours per week` IS A NUMBER
      `the relevant deductions` IS A NUMBER
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the claimant has taken all reasonable action for the purpose of obtaining paid work despite the number of hours that the claimant spends taking such action being lower than the expected number of hours per week` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that action gives the claimant the best prospects of obtaining work` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 95(1) — the claimant is treated as not having complied with the work search requirement to take all reasonable action` `the time which the claimant spends taking action for the purpose of obtaining paid work` `the expected number of hours per week` `the relevant deductions` `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the claimant has taken all reasonable action for the purpose of obtaining paid work despite the number of hours that the claimant spends taking such action being lower than the expected number of hours per week` `that action gives the claimant the best prospects of obtaining work` MEANS
    NOT (`enough time or satisfied` AND `that action gives the claimant the best prospects of obtaining work`)
    WHERE
        `enough time or satisfied` MEANS
            (`the time which the claimant spends taking action for the purpose of obtaining paid work` AT LEAST (`the expected number of hours per week` MINUS `the relevant deductions`))
            OR `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the claimant has taken all reasonable action for the purpose of obtaining paid work despite the number of hours that the claimant spends taking such action being lower than the expected number of hours per week`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulation 96 — Work availability requirement - able and willing immediately to take up paid work`

-- Paragraph (3): applies where (a) the claimant is a responsible carer or a relevant carer; (b) the Secretary of State is satisfied that, as a
-- consequence, the claimant needs a longer period of up to 1 month to take up paid work, or up to 48 hours to attend an interview, taking
-- into account alternative care arrangements; and (c) the claimant is able and willing to take up paid work, or attend an interview, on notice
-- for that period.
-- src:1474 | (3) This paragraph applies where—
-- src:1475 | (a) a claimant is a responsible carer or a relevant carer;
-- src:1476 | (b) the Secretary of State is satisfied that, as a consequence the claimant needs a longer period of up to 1 month to take up paid work, or up to 48 hours to attend an interview in connection with obtaining work, taking into account alternative care arrangements; and
-- src:1477 | (c) the claimant is able and willing to take up paid work, or attend an interview, on being given notice for that period.
@ref reg 96(3) (src:1474-1477)
GIVEN `the claimant is a responsible carer or a relevant carer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied that, as a consequence, the claimant needs a longer period of up to 1 month to take up paid work, or up to 48 hours to attend an interview, taking into account alternative care arrangements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is able and willing to take up paid work, or attend an interview, on being given notice for that period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 96(3) — this paragraph applies to a carer` `the claimant is a responsible carer or a relevant carer` `the Secretary of State is satisfied that, as a consequence, the claimant needs a longer period of up to 1 month to take up paid work, or up to 48 hours to attend an interview, taking into account alternative care arrangements` `the claimant is able and willing to take up paid work, or attend an interview, on being given notice for that period` MEANS
    `the claimant is a responsible carer or a relevant carer`
    AND `the Secretary of State is satisfied that, as a consequence, the claimant needs a longer period of up to 1 month to take up paid work, or up to 48 hours to attend an interview, taking into account alternative care arrangements`
    AND `the claimant is able and willing to take up paid work, or attend an interview, on being given notice for that period`

-- Paragraph (4): applies where (a) the claimant is carrying out voluntary work; (b) the Secretary of State is satisfied that, as a consequence,
-- the claimant needs a longer period of up to 1 week to take up paid work, or up to 48 hours to attend an interview; and (c) the claimant is
-- able and willing to take up paid work, or attend an interview, on notice for that period.
-- src:1478 | (4) This paragraph applies where—
-- src:1479 | (a) a claimant is carrying out voluntary work;
-- src:1480 | (b) the Secretary of State is satisfied that, as a consequence, the claimant needs a longer period of up to 1 week to take up paid work, or up to 48 hours to attend an interview in connection with obtaining work; and
-- src:1481 | (c) the claimant is able and willing to take up paid work, or attend an interview, on being given notice for that period.
@ref reg 96(4) (src:1478-1481)
GIVEN `the claimant is carrying out voluntary work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied that, as a consequence, the claimant needs a longer period of up to 1 week to take up paid work, or up to 48 hours to attend an interview` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is able and willing to take up paid work, or attend an interview, on being given notice for that period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 96(4) — this paragraph applies to a claimant doing voluntary work` `the claimant is carrying out voluntary work` `the Secretary of State is satisfied that, as a consequence, the claimant needs a longer period of up to 1 week to take up paid work, or up to 48 hours to attend an interview` `the claimant is able and willing to take up paid work, or attend an interview, on being given notice for that period` MEANS
    `the claimant is carrying out voluntary work`
    AND `the Secretary of State is satisfied that, as a consequence, the claimant needs a longer period of up to 1 week to take up paid work, or up to 48 hours to attend an interview`
    AND `the claimant is able and willing to take up paid work, or attend an interview, on being given notice for that period`

-- Paragraph (5): applies where a claimant (a) is employed under a contract of service; (b) is required by section 86 of the Employment Rights
-- Act 1996, or by the contract, to give notice to terminate it; (c) is able and willing to take up paid work once the notice period has
-- expired; and (d) is able and willing to attend an interview on 48 hours' notice.
-- out of range: sections 86 and 148 of the Employment Rights Act 1996 (not among the inputs): the facts they describe are stated inputs
-- src:1482 | (5) This paragraph applies where a claimant—
-- src:1483 | (a) is employed under a contract of service;
-- src:1484 | (b) is required by section 86 of the Employment Rights Act 1996 , or by the contract of service, to give notice to terminate the contract;
-- src:1485 | (c) is able and willing to take up paid work once the notice period has expired; and
-- src:1486 | (d) is able and willing to attend an interview on being given 48 hours notice.
@ref reg 96(5) (src:1482-1486)
GIVEN `the claimant is employed under a contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is required by section 86 of the Employment Rights Act 1996, or by the contract of service, to give notice to terminate the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is able and willing to take up paid work once the notice period has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is able and willing to attend an interview on being given 48 hours notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 96(5) — this paragraph applies to a claimant working out a notice period` `the claimant is employed under a contract of service` `the claimant is required by section 86 of the Employment Rights Act 1996, or by the contract of service, to give notice to terminate the contract` `the claimant is able and willing to take up paid work once the notice period has expired` `the claimant is able and willing to attend an interview on being given 48 hours notice` MEANS
    `the claimant is employed under a contract of service`
    AND `the claimant is required by section 86 of the Employment Rights Act 1996, or by the contract of service, to give notice to terminate the contract`
    AND `the claimant is able and willing to take up paid work once the notice period has expired`
    AND `the claimant is able and willing to attend an interview on being given 48 hours notice`

-- Paragraph (2): a claimant is treated as having complied with a work availability requirement despite not being able immediately to take up
-- paid work, if paragraph (3), (4) or (5) applies.
-- src:1473 | (2) But a claimant is to be treated as having complied with a work availability requirement despite not being able immediately to take up paid work, if paragraph (3), (4) or (5) applies.
@ref reg 96(2) (src:1473)
GIVEN `paragraph (3) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (4) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (5) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 96(2) — the claimant is treated as having complied despite not being able immediately to take up paid work` `paragraph (3) applies` `paragraph (4) applies` `paragraph (5) applies` MEANS
    `paragraph (3) applies` OR `paragraph (4) applies` OR `paragraph (5) applies`

-- Paragraph (1): subject to paragraph (2), a claimant is treated as not having complied with a work availability requirement if the claimant
-- is not able and willing immediately to attend an interview offered in connection with obtaining paid work. Paragraph (2) is read as
-- displacing paragraph (1) whenever it applies (fork F-96-1).
-- src:1471 | 96 Work availability requirement - able and willing immediately to take up paid work
-- src:1472 | (1) Subject to paragraph (2) a claimant is to be treated as not having complied with a work availability requirement if the claimant is not able and willing immediately to attend an interview offered to the claimant in connection with obtaining paid work.
@ref reg 96(1) (src:1471-1472)
GIVEN `the claimant is able and willing immediately to attend an interview offered in connection with obtaining paid work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (2) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 96(1) — the claimant is treated as not having complied with a work availability requirement` `the claimant is able and willing immediately to attend an interview offered in connection with obtaining paid work` `paragraph (2) applies` MEANS
    (NOT `the claimant is able and willing immediately to attend an interview offered in connection with obtaining paid work`)
    AND (NOT `paragraph (2) applies`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulation 97 — Work search requirement and work availability requirement - limitations`

-- Paragraph (2): in the case of a claimant who is a relevant carer or a responsible carer or who has a physical or mental impairment, a work
-- search and work availability requirement must be limited to the expected number of hours per week of regulation 88. For any other
-- claimant paragraph (2) sets no limit: the rule returns NOTHING.
-- src:1487 | 97 Work search requirement and work availability requirement - limitations
-- src:1488 | (1) Paragraphs (2) to (5) set out the limitations on a work search requirement and a work availability requirement.
-- src:1489 | (2) In the case of a claimant who is a relevant carer or a responsible carer or who has a physical or mental impairment, a work search and work availability requirement must be limited to the number of hours that is determined to be the claimant's expected number of hours per week in accordance with regulation 88.
@ref reg 97(1) and (2) (src:1487-1489)
GIVEN `the claimant is a relevant carer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is a responsible carer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant has a physical or mental impairment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the expected number of hours per week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 97(2) — the hours to which a work search and work availability requirement must be limited` `the claimant is a relevant carer` `the claimant is a responsible carer` `the claimant has a physical or mental impairment` `the expected number of hours per week` MEANS
    IF `the claimant is a relevant carer` OR `the claimant is a responsible carer` OR `the claimant has a physical or mental impairment`
    THEN JUST `the expected number of hours per week`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Paragraph (3): a work search and work availability requirement must be limited to work in a location that would normally take the
-- claimant a maximum of 90 minutes to travel from home to the location and a maximum of 90 minutes to travel from the location to home.
-- src:1490 | (3) A work search and work availability requirement must be limited to work that is in a location which would normally take the claimant—
-- src:1491 | (a) a maximum of 90 minutes to travel from home to the location; and
-- src:1492 | (b) a maximum of 90 minutes to travel from the location to home.
@ref reg 97(3) (src:1490-1492)
GIVEN `minutes that the location would normally take the claimant to travel from home` IS A NUMBER
      `minutes that the location would normally take the claimant to travel to home` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 97(3) — the location is within the travelling limit` `minutes that the location would normally take the claimant to travel from home` `minutes that the location would normally take the claimant to travel to home` MEANS
    (`minutes that the location would normally take the claimant to travel from home` AT MOST 90)
    AND (`minutes that the location would normally take the claimant to travel to home` AT MOST 90)

-- Paragraphs (4) and (5): where a claimant has previously carried out work of a particular nature, or at a particular level of remuneration,
-- the requirements must be limited to work of a similar nature or remuneration for such period as the Secretary of State considers
-- appropriate, but only if the Secretary of State is satisfied that the claimant will have reasonable prospects of obtaining paid work in spite of
-- the limitation; the limitation applies for no more than 4 weeks beginning with the date of claim or, if later, the date on which the claimant
-- ceases paid work after falling within section 19 of the Act by virtue of regulation 90. "No more than 4 weeks beginning with" is counted as
-- at most 28 days from the first of those days, both ends included (fork F-97-1).
-- out of range: sections 19, 20 and 22 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (not among the inputs): which work-related group the claimant is in is a stated input
-- src:1493 | (4) Where a claimant has previously carried out work of a particular nature, or at a particular level of remuneration, a work search requirement and a work availability requirement must be limited to work of a similar nature, or level of remuneration, for such period as the Secretary of State considers appropriate, but only if the Secretary of State is satisfied that the claimant will have reasonable prospects of obtaining paid work in spite of such limitation.
-- src:1494 | (5) The limitation in paragraph (4) is to apply for no more than 4 weeks beginning with—
-- src:1495 | (a) the date of claim; or
-- src:1496 | (b) if later, the date on which the claimant ceases paid work after falling within section 19 of the Act by virtue of regulation 90 (claimants subject to no work-related requirements - the earnings thresholds).
@ref reg 97(4) and (5) (src:1493-1496)
GIVEN `the claimant has previously carried out work of a particular nature, or at a particular level of remuneration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the claimant will have reasonable prospects of obtaining paid work in spite of such limitation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of claim` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the claimant ceases paid work after falling within section 19 of the Act by virtue of regulation 90` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the number of days for which the Secretary of State considers it appropriate that the limitation applies` IS A NUMBER
      `the date as at which it is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 97(4) and (5) — the work must be of a similar nature or remuneration` `the claimant has previously carried out work of a particular nature, or at a particular level of remuneration` `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the claimant will have reasonable prospects of obtaining paid work in spite of such limitation` `the date of claim` `the date on which the claimant ceases paid work after falling within section 19 of the Act by virtue of regulation 90` `the number of days for which the Secretary of State considers it appropriate that the limitation applies` `the date as at which it is asked` MEANS
    `the claimant has previously carried out work of a particular nature, or at a particular level of remuneration`
    AND `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the claimant will have reasonable prospects of obtaining paid work in spite of such limitation`
    AND (Day `the date as at which it is asked` MINUS Day `the day the period begins` AT LEAST 0)
    AND (Day `the date as at which it is asked` MINUS Day `the day the period begins` AT MOST (`the length of the period` MINUS 1))
    WHERE
        `the day the period begins` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the date on which the claimant ceases paid work after falling within section 19 of the Act by virtue of regulation 90`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `the date of claim`
            WHEN JUST ceased THEN
                IF Day ceased MINUS Day `the date of claim` AT LEAST 0 THEN ceased ELSE `the date of claim`
        `the length of the period` MEANS minimum (LIST `the number of days for which the Secretary of State considers it appropriate that the limitation applies`, 28)

-- Paragraph (6): where a claimant has a physical or mental impairment that has a substantial adverse effect on the claimant's ability to
-- carry out work of a particular nature, or in particular locations, a work search or work availability requirement must not relate to work of
-- such a nature or in such locations.
-- src:1497 | (6) Where a claimant has a physical or mental impairment that has a substantial adverse effect on the claimant's ability to carry out work of a particular nature, or in particular locations, a work search or work availability requirement must not relate to work of such a nature or in such locations.
@ref reg 97(6) (src:1497)
GIVEN `the claimant has a physical or mental impairment that has a substantial adverse effect on the claimant's ability to carry out work of a particular nature, or in particular locations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the work is of that nature or in those locations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 97(6) — a work search or work availability requirement must not relate to the work` `the claimant has a physical or mental impairment that has a substantial adverse effect on the claimant's ability to carry out work of a particular nature, or in particular locations` `the work is of that nature or in those locations` MEANS
    `the claimant has a physical or mental impairment that has a substantial adverse effect on the claimant's ability to carry out work of a particular nature, or in particular locations`
    AND `the work is of that nature or in those locations`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulation 98 — Victims of domestic violence`

-- Paragraph (4), "domestic violence": any incident, or pattern of incidents, of controlling behaviour, coercive behaviour, violence or abuse,
-- including but not limited to psychological, physical, sexual, emotional or financial abuse, regardless of the gender or sexuality of the victim.
-- "Controlling behaviour" is an act designed to make a person subordinate or dependent by isolating them from sources of support, exploiting
-- their resources and capacities for personal gain, depriving them of the means needed for independence, resistance or escape or
-- regulating their everyday behaviour. "Coercive behaviour" is an act of assault, humiliation or intimidation or other abuse that is used to
-- harm, punish or frighten the victim. Whether an incident is of a kind is a stated fact; the gender or sexuality of the victim is not a fact the
-- rule reads.
-- src:1511 | (4) In this regulation—
-- src:1512 | “coercive behaviour” means an act of assault, humiliation or intimidation or other abuse that is used to harm, punish or frighten the victim;
-- src:1513 | “controlling behaviour” means an act designed to make a person subordinate or dependent by isolating them from sources of support, exploiting their resources and capacities for personal gain, depriving them of the means needed for independence, resistance or escape or regulating their everyday behaviour;
-- src:1514 | “domestic violence” means any incident, or pattern of incidents, of controlling behaviour, coercive behaviour, violence or abuse, including but not limited to—
-- src:1515 | (a) psychological abuse;
-- src:1516 | (b) physical abuse;
-- src:1517 | (c) sexual abuse;
-- src:1518 | (d) emotional abuse;
-- src:1519 | (e) financial abuse,
-- src:1520 | regardless of the gender or sexuality of the victim;.
@ref reg 98(4) "coercive behaviour", "controlling behaviour", "domestic violence" (src:1511-1520)
DECLARE `Incident of domestic violence` HAS
    `the incident or pattern of incidents is controlling behaviour`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the incident or pattern of incidents is coercive behaviour`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the incident or pattern of incidents is violence`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the incident or pattern of incidents is abuse, including psychological, physical, sexual, emotional or financial abuse`   IS A BOOLEAN

@ref reg 98(4) "domestic violence" (src:1511-1520)
GIVEN incident IS AN `Incident of domestic violence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 98(4) — domestic violence` incident MEANS
    (incident's `the incident or pattern of incidents is controlling behaviour`)
    OR (incident's `the incident or pattern of incidents is coercive behaviour`)
    OR (incident's `the incident or pattern of incidents is violence`)
    OR (incident's `the incident or pattern of incidents is abuse, including psychological, physical, sexual, emotional or financial abuse`)

-- Paragraph (4), "family member", in relation to a claimant: the claimant's grandparent, grandchild, parent, step-parent, parent-in-law,
-- son, step-son, son-in-law, daughter, step-daughter, daughter-in-law, brother, step-brother, brother-in-law, sister, step-sister, sister-in-law
-- and, if any of those persons is a member of a couple, the other member of the couple. Compare the core's `Listed relation` for
-- "close relative" (a different list).
-- src:1521 | “family member”, in relation to a claimant, means the claimant's grandparent, grandchild, parent, step-parent, parent-in-law, son, step-son, son-in-law, daughter, step-daughter, daughter-in-law, brother, step-brother, brother-in-law, sister, step-sister, sister-in law and, if any of those persons is member of a couple, the other member of the couple;
@ref reg 98(4) "family member" (src:1521)
DECLARE `Relation of a family member to the claimant` IS ONE OF
    `a grandparent of the claimant`
    `a grandchild of the claimant`
    `a parent of the claimant`
    `a step-parent of the claimant`
    `a parent-in-law of the claimant`
    `a son of the claimant`
    `a step-son of the claimant`
    `a son-in-law of the claimant`
    `a daughter of the claimant`
    `a step-daughter of the claimant`
    `a daughter-in-law of the claimant`
    `a brother of the claimant`
    `a step-brother of the claimant`
    `a brother-in-law of the claimant`
    `a sister of the claimant`
    `a step-sister of the claimant`
    `a sister-in-law of the claimant`
    `not one of the relations of a family member`

DECLARE `Possible family member of the claimant` HAS
    `relation of the person to the claimant`                                  IS A `Relation of a family member to the claimant`
    `relation of the person's partner to the claimant`                        IS A `Relation of a family member to the claimant`

@ref reg 98(4) "family member" (src:1521)
GIVEN relative IS A `Possible family member of the claimant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 98(4) — family member` relative MEANS
    (NOT (relative's `relation of the person to the claimant` EQUALS `not one of the relations of a family member`))
    OR (NOT (relative's `relation of the person's partner to the claimant` EQUALS `not one of the relations of a family member`))

-- Paragraph (4), "person acting in an official capacity": a health care professional (in this regulation: a member of a profession regulated by a
-- body mentioned in section 25(3) of the National Health Service Reform and Health Care Professions Act 2002, not the core's meaning), a police
-- officer, a registered social worker (registered in a register maintained by Social Work England, Social Care Wales, the Scottish Social
-- Services Council or the Northern Ireland Social Care Council), the claimant's employer, a representative of the claimant's trade union, or any
-- public, voluntary or charitable body which has had direct contact with the claimant in connection with domestic violence.
-- out of range: section 25(3) of the National Health Service Reform and Health Care Professions Act 2002 (not among the inputs): the profession is a stated input
-- src:1522 | “health care professional” means a person who is a member of a profession regulated by a body mentioned in section 25(3) of the National Health Service Reform and Health Care Professions Act 2002 ;
-- src:1523 | “person acting in an official capacity” means a health care professional, a police officer, a registered social worker, the claimant's employer, a representative of the claimant's trade union, or any public, voluntary or charitable body which has had direct contact with the claimant in connection with domestic violence;
-- src:1524 | “registered social worker” means a person registered as a social worker in a register maintained by—
-- src:1525 | (a) Social Work England;
-- src:1526 | (b) Social Care Wales;
-- src:1527 | (c) The Scottish Social Services Council; or
-- src:1528 | (d) The Northern Ireland Social Care Council.
@ref reg 98(4) "health care professional", "person acting in an official capacity", "registered social worker" (src:1522-1528)
DECLARE `Person acting in an official capacity facts` HAS
    `a member of a profession regulated by a body mentioned in section 25(3) of the National Health Service Reform and Health Care Professions Act 2002`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `a police officer`                                                                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `registered as a social worker in a register maintained by Social Work England`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `registered as a social worker in a register maintained by Social Care Wales`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `registered as a social worker in a register maintained by the Scottish Social Services Council`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `registered as a social worker in a register maintained by the Northern Ireland Social Care Council`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant's employer`                                                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `a representative of the claimant's trade union`                                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `a public, voluntary or charitable body which has had direct contact with the claimant in connection with domestic violence`   IS A BOOLEAN

@ref reg 98(4) "person acting in an official capacity" (src:1522-1528)
GIVEN person IS A `Person acting in an official capacity facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 98(4) — person acting in an official capacity` person MEANS
    any (GIVEN limb YIELD limb)
        (LIST person's `a member of a profession regulated by a body mentioned in section 25(3) of the National Health Service Reform and Health Care Professions Act 2002`,
              person's `a police officer`,
              person's `registered as a social worker in a register maintained by Social Work England`,
              person's `registered as a social worker in a register maintained by Social Care Wales`,
              person's `registered as a social worker in a register maintained by the Scottish Social Services Council`,
              person's `registered as a social worker in a register maintained by the Northern Ireland Social Care Council`,
              person's `the claimant's employer`,
              person's `a representative of the claimant's trade union`,
              person's `a public, voluntary or charitable body which has had direct contact with the claimant in connection with domestic violence`)

-- Paragraph (2): a person has recently been a victim of domestic violence if a period of 6 months has not expired since the violence was
-- inflicted or threatened. The period of 6 months begins on the date of the violence, so it has expired on the same date six months later
-- (fork F-98-1).
-- src:1503 | (2) A person has recently been a victim of domestic violence if a period of 6 months has not expired since the violence was inflicted or threatened.
@ref reg 98(2) (src:1503)
GIVEN `date on which the violence was inflicted or threatened` IS A DATE
      `the date as at which it is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 98(2) — the claimant has recently been a victim of domestic violence` `date on which the violence was inflicted or threatened` `the date as at which it is asked` MEANS
    ((Day `the date as at which it is asked` MINUS Day `date on which the violence was inflicted or threatened`) AT LEAST 0)
    AND ((Day `the date as at which it is asked` MINUS Day (`core — the date reached by adding a time limit to a date` `date on which the violence was inflicted or threatened` (`Time limit` WITH quantity IS 6, unit IS months))) LESS THAN 0)

-- Paragraph (3): the circumstances are that (a) the claimant notifies the Secretary of State, in the manner specified, that domestic violence has
-- been inflicted on or threatened against the claimant by the claimant's partner or former partner or by a family member during the period of
-- 6 months ending on the date of the notification; (b) this regulation has not applied to the claimant for 12 months before the date of the
-- notification; (c) on the date of the notification the claimant is not living at the same address as the person who inflicted or threatened the
-- violence; and (d) as soon as possible, and no later than 1 month after the notification, the claimant provides evidence from a person acting
-- in an official capacity which demonstrates (i) that the claimant's circumstances are consistent with those of a person who has had domestic
-- violence inflicted or threatened against them in the 6 months ending on the date of the notification, and (ii) that the claimant has made
-- contact with that person in relation to such an incident, which occurred during that period.
-- src:1504 | (3) The circumstances are that—
-- src:1505 | (a) the claimant notifies the Secretary of State, in such manner as the Secretary of State specifies, that domestic violence has been inflicted on or threatened against the claimant by the claimant's partner or former partner or by a family member during the period of 6 months ending on the date of the notification;
-- src:1506 | (b) this regulation has not applied to the claimant for a period of 12 months before the date of the notification;
-- src:1507 | (c) on the date of the notification the claimant is not living at the same address as the person who inflicted or threatened the domestic violence; and
-- src:1508 | (d) as soon as possible, and no later than 1 month, after the date of the notification the claimant provides evidence from a person acting in an official capacity which demonstrates that—
-- src:1509 | (i) the claimant's circumstances are consistent with those of a person who has had domestic violence inflicted or threatened against them during the period of 6 months ending on the date of the notification, and
-- src:1510 | (ii) the claimant has made contact with the person acting in an official capacity in relation to such an incident, which occurred during that period.
@ref reg 98(3) (src:1504-1510)
DECLARE `Domestic violence notification facts` HAS
    `date of the notification`                                                                                                                         IS A DATE
    `the claimant notifies the Secretary of State, in such manner as the Secretary of State specifies, that domestic violence has been inflicted on or threatened against the claimant`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the incident is domestic violence`                                                                                                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `date on which the violence was inflicted or threatened`                                                                                           IS A DATE
    `the violence was inflicted or threatened by the claimant's partner or former partner`                                                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the violence was inflicted or threatened by a family member`                                                                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `last day on which this regulation applied to the claimant`                                                                                        IS A MAYBE DATE
    `on the date of the notification the claimant is living at the same address as the person who inflicted or threatened the domestic violence`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `date on which the claimant provided the evidence`                                                                                                 IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the claimant provided the evidence as soon as possible`                                                                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the evidence is from a person acting in an official capacity`                                                                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the evidence demonstrates that the claimant's circumstances are consistent with those of a person who has had domestic violence inflicted or threatened against them during the period of 6 months ending on the date of the notification`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the evidence demonstrates that the claimant has made contact with the person acting in an official capacity in relation to such an incident, which occurred during that period`   IS A BOOLEAN

@ref reg 98(3)(a) (src:1504-1505)
GIVEN facts IS A `Domestic violence notification facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 98(3)(a) — the claimant has notified the Secretary of State of domestic violence in the last 6 months` facts MEANS
    (facts's `the claimant notifies the Secretary of State, in such manner as the Secretary of State specifies, that domestic violence has been inflicted on or threatened against the claimant`)
    AND (facts's `the incident is domestic violence`)
    AND ((facts's `the violence was inflicted or threatened by the claimant's partner or former partner`) OR (facts's `the violence was inflicted or threatened by a family member`))
    AND (`reg 98(2) — the claimant has recently been a victim of domestic violence` (facts's `date on which the violence was inflicted or threatened`) (facts's `date of the notification`))

-- Limb (b): this regulation has not applied for 12 months before the notification. It is read as: the twelve months after the last day on which
-- it applied have run out by the date of the notification, the notification date itself counting (fork F-98-2).
@ref reg 98(3)(b) (src:1506)
GIVEN facts IS A `Domestic violence notification facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 98(3)(b) — this regulation has not applied to the claimant for 12 months` facts MEANS
    CONSIDER facts's `last day on which this regulation applied to the claimant`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST last THEN
        (Day (facts's `date of the notification`) MINUS Day (`core — the date reached by adding a time limit to a date` last (`Time limit` WITH quantity IS 12, unit IS months))) AT LEAST 0

@ref reg 98(3)(c) (src:1507)
GIVEN facts IS A `Domestic violence notification facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 98(3)(c) — the claimant is not living at the same address` facts MEANS
    NOT (facts's `on the date of the notification the claimant is living at the same address as the person who inflicted or threatened the domestic violence`)

-- Limb (d): the evidence is provided as soon as possible and no later than 1 month after the date of the notification.
@ref reg 98(3)(d) (src:1508-1510)
GIVEN facts IS A `Domestic violence notification facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 98(3)(d) — the claimant provides the evidence in time` facts MEANS
    (facts's `the claimant provided the evidence as soon as possible`)
    AND (facts's `the evidence is from a person acting in an official capacity`)
    AND (facts's `the evidence demonstrates that the claimant's circumstances are consistent with those of a person who has had domestic violence inflicted or threatened against them during the period of 6 months ending on the date of the notification`)
    AND (facts's `the evidence demonstrates that the claimant has made contact with the person acting in an official capacity in relation to such an incident, which occurred during that period`)
    AND `within 1 month after the notification`
    WHERE
        `within 1 month after the notification` MEANS
            CONSIDER facts's `date on which the claimant provided the evidence`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST provided THEN
                ((Day provided MINUS Day (facts's `date of the notification`)) AT LEAST 0)
                AND ((Day provided MINUS Day (`core — the date reached by adding a time limit to a date` (facts's `date of the notification`) (`Time limit` WITH quantity IS 1, unit IS months))) AT MOST 0)

@ref reg 98(3) (src:1504-1510)
GIVEN facts IS A `Domestic violence notification facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 98(3) — the circumstances apply` facts MEANS
    (`reg 98(3)(a) — the claimant has notified the Secretary of State of domestic violence in the last 6 months` facts)
    AND (`reg 98(3)(b) — this regulation has not applied to the claimant for 12 months` facts)
    AND (`reg 98(3)(c) — the claimant is not living at the same address` facts)
    AND (`reg 98(3)(d) — the claimant provides the evidence in time` facts)

-- Paragraph (1): where the claimant has recently been a victim of domestic violence and the circumstances in paragraph (3) apply, (a) a
-- work-related requirement imposed on the claimant ceases to have effect for 13 consecutive weeks starting on the date of the notification, and
-- (b) the Secretary of State must not impose any other work-related requirement on the claimant during that period. 13 weeks are 91 days,
-- the first of them the date of the notification.
-- src:1498 | 98 Victims of domestic violence
-- src:1499 | (1) Where a claimant has recently been a victim of domestic violence, and the circumstances set out in paragraph (3) apply—
-- src:1500 | (a) a work-related requirement imposed on that claimant ceases to have effect for a period of 13 consecutive weeks starting on the date of the notification referred to in paragraph (3)(a); and
-- src:1501 | (b) the Secretary of State must not impose any other work-related requirement on that claimant during that period.
@ref reg 98(1) (src:1498-1501)
GIVEN facts IS A `Domestic violence notification facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 98(1) — this regulation applies to the claimant` facts MEANS
    (`reg 98(2) — the claimant has recently been a victim of domestic violence` (facts's `date on which the violence was inflicted or threatened`) (facts's `date of the notification`))
    AND (`reg 98(3) — the circumstances apply` facts)

@ref reg 98(1)(a) (src:1498-1501)
GIVEN `this regulation applies to the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `date of the notification` IS A DATE
      `the date as at which it is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 98(1)(a) — a work-related requirement imposed on the claimant has no effect on the date` `this regulation applies to the claimant` `date of the notification` `the date as at which it is asked` MEANS
    `this regulation applies to the claimant`
    AND ((Day `the date as at which it is asked` MINUS Day `date of the notification`) AT LEAST 0)
    AND ((Day `the date as at which it is asked` MINUS Day `date of the notification`) AT MOST 90)

@ref reg 98(1)(b) (src:1498-1501)
GIVEN `this regulation applies to the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `date of the notification` IS A DATE
      `the date as at which it is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 98(1)(b) — the Secretary of State must not impose another work-related requirement on the date` `this regulation applies to the claimant` `date of the notification` `the date as at which it is asked` MEANS
    `this regulation applies to the claimant`
    AND ((Day `the date as at which it is asked` MINUS Day `date of the notification`) AT LEAST 0)
    AND ((Day `the date as at which it is asked` MINUS Day `date of the notification`) AT MOST 90)

-- Paragraph (1A): where a claimant referred to in paragraph (1) falls within section 22 of the Act and is the responsible carer of a child, the
-- Secretary of State must not impose a work search or work availability requirement for a further 13 consecutive weeks beginning on the day
-- after the period in paragraph (1)(a) expires: the 91 days that begin 91 days after the date of the notification.
-- out of range: sections 19, 20 and 22 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (not among the inputs): which work-related group the claimant is in is a stated input
-- src:1502 | (1A) Where a claimant referred to in paragraph (1) is a person who falls within section 22 of the Act (claimants subject to all work-related requirements) and is the responsible carer of a child, the Secretary of State must not impose a work search requirement or a work availability requirement on that claimant for a further period of 13 consecutive weeks beginning on the day after the period in paragraph (1)(a) expires.
@ref reg 98(1A) (src:1502)
GIVEN `this regulation applies to the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant falls within section 22 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is the responsible carer of a child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `date of the notification` IS A DATE
      `the date as at which it is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 98(1A) — the Secretary of State must not impose a work search or work availability requirement on the date` `this regulation applies to the claimant` `the claimant falls within section 22 of the Act` `the claimant is the responsible carer of a child` `date of the notification` `the date as at which it is asked` MEANS
    `this regulation applies to the claimant`
    AND `the claimant falls within section 22 of the Act`
    AND `the claimant is the responsible carer of a child`
    AND ((Day `the date as at which it is asked` MINUS Day `date of the notification`) AT LEAST 91)
    AND ((Day `the date as at which it is asked` MINUS Day `date of the notification`) AT MOST 181)
